<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index < i && i < this.size(); (this.get(i) != null || \old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))));</code>

Explanation:
- The assertion checks if the index is valid (non-negative and less than the initial size of the list).
- It then asserts that for every index `i` greater than the specified index and less than the current size of the list, the element at that index remains unchanged unless it was initially `null`. This is captured using the condition `(this.get(i) != null || \old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))))`. This ensures that if the element was `null`, it can remain `null`, otherwise, it must be equal to its old value.
